Binary OPENSTEP nib support
==========================

The private typedstream reader in this directory is adapted from
NIBMAKER-FOR-OPENSTEP, commit bcc7c1a09e0be874f1df259e809517a89b765986
(src/ts_read.c, src/ts_read.h, src/ts_types.h).  That project's LICENSE is
the GNU Library General Public License version 2.  Preserve its original
format documentation when updating this copy.  No XML reader, XML writer,
typedstream writer, preview renderer, or external executable is linked.

Local adaptations:
  - Prefix external functions with GSOpenStepTS; remove file I/O and tracing.
  - Bound recursive values/classes/type encodings, allocation and array counts.
  - Use subtraction for input bounds checks, avoiding addition overflow.

GSOpenStepNibReader.m translates the binary graph into an in-memory binary
keyed archive.  It does not execute application initializers.  GSNibLoader
then uses its existing NSKeyedUnarchiver / NSIBObjectData path, including
owner substitution, connections, top-level ownership and awakeFromNib.
Fractional button repeat intervals are applied using public NSButtonCell
methods immediately before awakening.  No GUI element class is modified.

Detection and bundles
---------------------
Recognize streamer versions 3 and 4, signature length 11, and either
streamtyped (little endian) or typedstream (big endian).  Recognition is
only a routing decision: the reader must still validate the entire input.
Keyed binary and XML nibs retain their existing separate loading path.
NIBMAKER's XML projection is not accepted.

Directory payload preference is keyedobjects.nib, objects.nib, data.nib.
Once a payload exists, failure to read/decode it is an error; do not silently
fall back to an older interface in the same bundle.  Raw .nib files and
NSNib's NSData initializer use the same format dispatch.

Current semantic coverage and limits
-----------------------------------
This is native OPENSTEP support for the following measured class versions,
not a claim to support every archive ever emitted by NeXT or Apple:

  NSObject 0; NSString 1; NSArray/NSMutableArray/NSSet/NSMutableSet 0
  NSIBObjectData 24; NSCustomObject/NSCustomResource 41
  NSIBConnector 17; NSIBOutletConnector/NSIBControlConnector 0
  NSResponder 0; NSView/NSControl/NSCustomView 41
  NSWindowTemplate 41; NSButton 0; NSTextField 25
  NSCell 60; NSActionCell 17; NSButtonCell 57; NSTextFieldCell 61
  NSBox 41; NSMatrix 60; NSFont 21; NSColor 0

The field layouts come from the upstream doc/WIDGETS.md, nib_parse.c and
gen-widget-nib.py.  Group encodings, counts, inheritance versions and trailing
groups are checked.  Unknown classes encountered anywhere in the graph fail
before any application object is instantiated, with class/version/offset
diagnostics.  Do not map an unknown class to NSView or silently drop its state.

Known limitations are explicit in the adapter:
  - Unprefixed NeXTSTEP AppKit (IBObjectData, View, Cell, etc.) has different
    layouts and is not supported, even when packaged in an OPENSTEP app.
  - Nonzero historical NSView flags, transforms/auxiliary view state, window
    size extensions, nonzero font roles, and unknown container sections are
    rejected pending measured mappings.  They must not be copied into modern
    flags merely because the field names resemble each other.
  - Menus, popups, scroll views, browsers and other unlisted classes need
    separate adapters.  Custom view/object placeholders are supported;
    arbitrary archived application subclass state is not.
  - Strings use NEXTSTEP encoding.  Archives containing application-specific
    encodings such as EUC-KR need explicit encoding support.

Tests
-----
Tests/gui/NSNibLoading/make-openstep-fixtures.py creates original binary
fixtures without an XML intermediate or proprietary source material.
openstep.m exercises the real loader and NSNib lifecycle; --gui also checks
window templates, controls, action delivery, identity, geometry and timing.
typedstream.c exercises truncation, mutated input, random bytes and limits
and can be built with AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.

The upstream checkout used for this implementation does not contain the
original OPENSTEP fixture corpus.  Validation against original application
nibs, and expanding the measured layout coverage, remain necessary before
claiming general OPENSTEP compatibility.
